WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.460
A few years ago, I was in Hong Kong. I was&nbsp;
doing a story for Vox and I went to this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:09.780
giant bridge and I flew my drone over it and it&nbsp;
was this big story. And a while back I was like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:13.440
does the United States have any big super&nbsp;
cool bridges that do all this cool stuff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:17.340
like in the ocean? Turns out we do. It's&nbsp;
not nearly as big, but we have this bridge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:23.400
the Chesapeake Bridge, which is four and a half&nbsp;
miles long. And apparently it's the scariest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.540
bridge in America. I've driven over this bridge&nbsp;
a bunch because it's like 20 miles from my house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.840
and I never thought it was that scary. But&nbsp;
apparently a lot of people think it's really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:36.240
scary, so much so that there's an entire service&nbsp;
where you could go show up with your car and there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:40.440
will be someone waiting for you and they will&nbsp;
get in your car and they will drive you across&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:45.480
the bridge if you're afraid. So we have ourselves&nbsp;
a nice big bridge that's apparently super scary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:50.820
because there's nowhere to pull off on. And if&nbsp;
you need to go across it, there is someone there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:55.440
that will do it for you. And they've got a great&nbsp;
infomercial in case you need to be convinced.

